{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0088", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}^\\#$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\#$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\mathcal{O}^\\# \\times \\mathcal{F}^\\#\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{F}^\\#\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{O} \\times \\mathcal{F} \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\mathcal{F} \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\mathcal{O}^\\# \\times \\mathcal{F}^\\# \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{F}^\\#\n}\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\#$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{O}^\\#$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{O}^\\#$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F}^\\# \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\# \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{O}^\\#$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-sheafification-presheaf-modules}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:64f99a15ee9f9c74a2dddfe3438cca37936f0d6bc7efff386ea1ed9b823d4719", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f1d7fb4f637bee628a80f37da7d370c19f35cdc8ad24df583d80b8de9f3cb88d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a topological space.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a presheaf of rings on <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a presheaf of <MATH_0005>-modules.\nLet <MATH_0006> be the sheafification of <MATH_0007>.\nLet <MATH_0008> be the sheafification of <MATH_0009>\nas a presheaf of abelian groups. There exists a map of\nsheaves of sets\n<MATH_0010>\nwhich makes the diagram\n<MATH_0011>\ncommute and which makes <MATH_0012> into a sheaf\nof <MATH_0013>-modules. In addition, if <MATH_0014>\nis a sheaf of <MATH_0015>-modules, then any morphism\nof presheaves of <MATH_0016>-modules <MATH_0017>\n(into the restriction of <MATH_0018> to a <MATH_0019>-module)\nfactors uniquely as <MATH_0020>\nwhere <MATH_0021> is a morphism of\n<MATH_0022>-modules.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f8f9068f2ae3a9eb592cb4e578353e573897861f11c4721480968521ca88306b", "unit_id": "tag:0089:statement"}
