{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0088", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i : \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}^\\#) \\to \\textit{PMod}(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "${}^\\# : \\textit{PMod}(\\mathcal{O}) \\to \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}^\\#)$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PMod}(\\mathcal{O})}(\\mathcal{F}, i\\mathcal{G})\n=\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}^\\#)}(\\mathcal{F}^\\#, \\mathcal{G})\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_1 \\to \\mathcal{O}_2$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_2$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{F}_{\\mathcal{O}_1}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{O}_1$", "MATH_0012": "$$\n\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_2)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_1)\n$$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{O}_1$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{O}_2$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{O}_2 \\otimes_{p, \\mathcal{O}_1} \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{O}_2 \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_1} \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0018": "$$\n\\mathcal{O}_2 \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_1} \\mathcal{G}\n=\n(\\mathcal{O}_2 \\otimes_{p, \\mathcal{O}_1} \\mathcal{G})^\\#\n$$", "MATH_0019": "$$\n\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_1)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_2)\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-presheaves-modules}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0005": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0006": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0007": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:151d9315f20e55f42a051c45f7fecb39041a22b013ef5e6d1f4e1aae57e2cfcd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:393a5bb9202a101c52a9b9c0a45700befb371e33aa3912336e6fff0ad98e0686", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis actually means that the functor\n<MATH_0001>\n(combining restriction and including sheaves into presheaves)\nand the sheafification functor of the lemma\n<MATH_0002>\nare adjoint. In a formula\n<MATH_0003>\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nLet <MATH_0004> be a topological space.\nLet <MATH_0005> be\na morphism of sheaves of rings on <MATH_0006>.\nIn Section <REF_0001>\nwe defined a restriction functor\nand a change of rings functor on presheaves of modules\nassociated to this situation.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nIf <MATH_0007> is a sheaf of <MATH_0008>-modules\nthen the restriction <MATH_0009>\nof <MATH_0010> is clearly a sheaf\nof <MATH_0011>-modules. We obtain the restriction functor\n<MATH_0012>\n\n<STRUCT_0006><STRUCT_0007>\nOn the other hand, given a sheaf of <MATH_0013>-modules\n<MATH_0014> the presheaf of <MATH_0015>-modules\n<MATH_0016>\nis in general not a sheaf. Hence we define the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>tensor product sheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\n<MATH_0017>\nby the formula\n<MATH_0018>\nas the sheafification of our construction for presheaves.\nWe obtain the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>change of rings<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> functor\n<MATH_0019>\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:36f9fde14b655ef20bccb18becc6c43b44151bc259a874036d79e8be4c02c09f", "unit_id": "tag:0088:prose-0001"}
